From 48e061e62c8ab417b0f94bec6ed1e284f5bcc420 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BaptGosse <baptiste.gosselin@unxwares.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:49:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] chore(deps): update golang.org/x/crypto and the archive
 modules

Image scanners and govulncheck report these modules of the 4.19.1 build:

- golang.org/x/crypto v0.58.0 (GO-2026-5932, the deprecated openpgp
  packages, removed in v0.59.0; Cloudreve does not import them)
- github.com/nwaples/rardecode/v2 v2.1.0 (CVE-2025-11579)
- github.com/klauspost/compress v1.18.7 (GO-2026-6865, CVE-2026-116591)
- github.com/andybalholm/brotli v1.1.2-0.20250424173009-453214e765f3
  (GO-2026-6888, CVE-2026-111497)

rardecode v2.2.0 needs github.com/mholt/archives v0.1.5, which drops the
WriterTo constraint of its RAR reader. The archives API that Cloudreve
uses (Identify, Extractor, Zip.TextEncoding, Rar.Password,
SevenZip.Password, FileInfo) is unchanged. go mod tidy moves the other
modules with them.

github.com/mojocn/base64Captcha stays at the 2019 version: 1.3.x, which
fixes CVE-2023-45292, no longer has the API that Cloudreve uses
(ConfigCharacter, GenerateCaptcha, VerifyCaptcha,
CaptchaWriteToBase64Encoding). The vulnerable function,
memoryStore.Verify, does not exist in the 2019 version, and its
VerifyCaptcha refuses an empty answer.

Signed-off-by: BaptGosse <baptiste.gosselin@unxwares.com>
